{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:finite-sieve-honest-consistent-upper",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "There exists \\(n_0<\\infty\\), depending only on \\(\\alpha\\) and the fixed class indices, such that for every \\(n\\ge n_0\\) the finite-dimensional, semi-infinite deterministic profiling construction \\(\\mathfrak H^{\\mathrm{up}}\\) yields a band \\(\\mathcal C_n\\in\\mathfrak B_{n,\\alpha}\\) with jointly sample-and-index measurable finite endpoints, simultaneous coverage at least \\(1-\\alpha\\) uniformly over \\(\\mathcal M\\), and \\(0\\le W_n\\le2B_Y\\) almost surely. Moreover,\n\\[\n \\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M}E_{P_{\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}}[W_n]\n \\le \\widetilde\\omega_n+2b_{\\mu,n}\n   +2B_Y|\\mathcal X|e^{-np_{\\min}/8}=o(1).\n\\]\nNo finite decision algorithm is claimed. The conclusion is qualitative and gives neither an explicit rate, an \\(O(r_n)\\) bound, nor a minimax claim.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak H^{\\mathrm{up}}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal C_n\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak B_{n,\\alpha}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M\\)",
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(P_{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)",
      "\\(L_n\\)",
      "\\(U_n\\)",
      "\\(\\mu\\)",
      "\\(I\\)",
      "\\(W_n\\)",
      "\\(B_Y\\)",
      "\\(\\widetilde\\omega_n\\)",
      "\\(b_{\\mu,n}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal X\\)",
      "\\(p_{\\min}\\)",
      "\\(r_n\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:honest-bands",
      "def:profiled-band",
      "def:finite-sieve-diameter",
      "thm:honest-upper",
      "lem:finite-sieve-diameter",
      "lem:mass-confidence"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "All measurability, ordering, clipping, honesty, and coverage assertions follow from \\(\\mathrm{thm{:}honest\\text{-}upper}\\). Let\n\\[\n \\mathcal R_n=\\{\\min_{x\\in\\mathcal X}n_x\\ge np_{\\min}/2\\}.\n\\]\nOn \\(\\mathcal R_n\\), an empty feasible set gives \\(W_n=0\\). If the feasible set is nonempty, put\n\\[\n \\ell(a)=\\inf_{\\theta\\in\\Theta_{n,\\alpha}}\\mu_\\theta(a),\n \\qquad\n u(a)=\\sup_{\\theta\\in\\Theta_{n,\\alpha}}\\mu_\\theta(a).\n\\]\nSince \\(L_n(a)\\ge\\ell(a)-b_{\\mu,n}\\) and \\(U_n(a)\\le u(a)+b_{\\mu,n}\\),\n\\[\n U_n(a)-L_n(a)\\le u(a)-\\ell(a)+2b_{\\mu,n}.\n\\]\nTaking the supremum over \\(I\\) and using the finite-sieve diameter gives\n\\[\n W_n\\mathbf1_{\\mathcal R_n}\\le\\widetilde\\omega_n+2b_{\\mu,n}.\n\\]\nOn \\(\\mathcal R_n^c\\), clipping gives \\(W_n\\le2B_Y\\). The count inequality in \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}mass\\text{-}confidence}\\) therefore gives, uniformly over \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\),\n\\[\n E_{P_{\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}}[W_n]\n \\le\\widetilde\\omega_n+2b_{\\mu,n}\n   +2B_Y|\\mathcal X|e^{-np_{\\min}/8}.\n\\]\nThe finite-sieve diameter tends to zero. Also \\(b_{\\mu,n}\\to0\\), because it is a fixed positive linear combination of \\(K_n^{1/2-\\beta}\\) terms and \\(\\beta>1/2\\); the exponential remainder also vanishes. Hence the displayed bound is \\(o(1)\\). No step supplies a quantitative rate for \\(\\widetilde\\omega_n\\).",
    "justification": "The finite-dimensional, semi-infinite empirical-characteristic-function profiling band is uniformly honest and has uniformly vanishing expected maximal width under the same assumptions.",
    "gap": "The theorem proves \\(o(1)\\) but not \\(O(r_n)\\); tightness and the fixed-nuisance marked converse remain open.",
    "consumer": "It provides qualitative whole-curve uncertainty quantification while separating consistency from the unresolved sharp-rate program.",
